Executables here run before the UPS Safe Mode stops the services (synodeb-ups), in name
order, with the reason (lowbatt, waittimeup, nocomm, fsd, shutdowncmd) as $1, all together
within PRE_SAFEMODE_TIMEOUT seconds (/etc/synodeb/ups.conf, default 120). Names: letters,
digits, - and _ only (this file is not executable and not run). Output goes to the journal
(journalctl -t synodeb-ups-hook). Example, 10-containers:

    #!/bin/sh
    docker ps -q | xargs -r docker stop -t 30
